From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:15:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] power: Normalize ambient brightness baseline to neutral 50%

gnome-shell's BrightnessManager applies the auto-brightness target as a
bias centered at 0.5:

  target = clamp(abTarget + scale.value - 0.5, 0.0, 1.0)

gsd-power normalized the initial ambient reading with factor 1.5, which
produced an initial ambient target of 100 / 1.5 = 66.7% (0.667). On every
session login under constant light this added +16.7% to the restored
brightness, ratcheting the display toward maximum across reboots and
preventing the slider from reaching the bottom of the backlight range.
In addition, re-normalizing after a manual user adjustment left the old
ambient_accumulator in place so the filter kept pushing against the user's
chosen level.

Use a normalization factor of 2.0 (baseline 50% = 0.5) and reset
ambient_accumulator and ambient_update_last_time on re-normalization so
constant room light keeps the user's or restored brightness unchanged and
the full 0..100% range remains reachable.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
diff --git a/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c b/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
index 7d57383..0c668c7 100644
--- a/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
+++ b/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
@@ -95,9 +95,10 @@
  * for us in the future so we can drop this value to ~1 time per second. */
 #define GSD_AMBIENT_SEND_UPDATE_INTERVAL (G_USEC_PER_SEC * 0.1f)
 
-/* Normalize against this factor of the current absolute reading.
- * The value has been chosen arbitrarily but seems to work in practice. */
-#define GSD_AMBIENT_NORMALIZE_CONSTANT (1.5f)
+/* Normalize against twice the current absolute reading so the baseline
+ * ambient target is 50% (0.5), matching gnome-shell's neutral bias point
+ * (target = clamp(abTarget + scale.value - 0.5, 0, 1)). */
+#define GSD_AMBIENT_NORMALIZE_CONSTANT (2.0f)
 
 static const gchar introspection_xml[] =
 "<node>"
@@ -2974,8 +2975,8 @@ iio_proxy_changed (GsdPowerManager *manager)
                 g_debug ("Normalizing light level");
 
                 manager->ambient_norm_value = ambient_last_absolute * GSD_AMBIENT_NORMALIZE_CONSTANT;
-                if (manager->ambient_accumulator <= 0.f)
-                        manager->ambient_accumulator = 100.f / GSD_AMBIENT_NORMALIZE_CONSTANT;
+                manager->ambient_accumulator = 100.f / GSD_AMBIENT_NORMALIZE_CONSTANT;
+                manager->ambient_update_last_time = 0;
 
                 manager->ambient_norm_required = FALSE;
         }
